sasha it has been a long time coming i'm  excited to talk to you thank you for  having me  for people who do not know where did the  idea for nightgowns come from  five years ago well it actually all  started with  this magazine that my partner johnny and  i started producing in brooklyn it was  our way  to like get to know the local scene and  also  to merge our two worlds of drag and of  illustration and design and photography  and so we started this project that  celebrated all the different  styles and artistry of drag trying to  create drag  for the printed page i guess and we  ended up just throwing  a party to help sell the magazine found  a bar that would allow us to do it  and the bar owners basically said like  that was such a great show would you  consider doing that every month  and that was the birth of nightgowns it  started small and just kept growing  and my time on drag race just fueled my  passion  and like my maybe ambitions in some ways  with what nightgowns could be and now  it's a quippy  documentary it just kept going we're  transforming  the system that doesn't work for us  meticulousness is the thing that has  made her successful everybody was just  obsessed with the series when it came  out  tell me how did it feel to have it so  well received by not only your fan base  but also critics  i mean because it's such a personal  project for all of the performers  and then to share it with everyone and  not just what we share on nightgowns  which is the  kind of polished surface beautiful  performative side of drag but  to kind of be bold enough to pull back  the curtain and show  like some of the insecurities some of  the nerves backstage  um some of the unfinished um imperfect  aspects i think that was  kind of something really new for all of  us we aren't interested  in the world as it is we are interested  in the world  as it could be nothing feels more alive  than that i think i know the answer to  this but tell me are you game for a  season two  hello yes obviously i think we would  know just what to do with  it oh every time we have an opportunity  to put on the show we try to deliver  well big exciting news on august 9th  there is going to be  a three hour digital drag performance  live stream called night gowns forever  featuring  30 incredible sets from some of your  favorite drag performers  sasha tell me how did it feel to go back  and watch some of these old  performances from you know even five  years ago i  imagine it was kind of emotional for you  it was amazing when we were getting  ready for the  for the season on quibby we tried to  gather all the archival materials they  were like  mainly on one hard drive they kept  changing hands and when it came back we  realized with so  much material like incredible  performances  from three years ago two years ago just  from a couple months ago  and the star of those performances was  the audience in many ways and the  amazing interaction that always happens  at nighttime  between a performer just like bringing  their best the gorgeous life that i try  to keep for them  and the audience screaming their heads  off and i was like  we could really turn this into something  all this footage that we just had  i love that the event is free of charge  because they be entertained to feel  things right  that's exactly it but for those who are  watching and can make a donation it is  going to go to some great causes for  black lives  and black trans lives um sasha i love  that thank you for doing that  tell me when you look at the state of  the world right now  in 2020 you know there's a lot going on  there's a lot of movements in grassroots  protesters and  activists using their voice are you  feeling hopeful  absolutely like you said hopeful i i was  standing  in the sea of many many queer people  just a couple blocks away outside the  brooklyn museum for the  brooklyn action for black trans lives  which was organized in part by  a drag artist west dakota um who  whose performance appears in nightcast  forever i  feel hope that um there can be  real substantive change and i'm excited  for the ways in which in our own  communities  like we are trying to think of what that  means  not just talking about it i think people  are gonna see some real changes  i'm i'm gonna be a part of it so i'm  excited  as a friend of shae um you know she  spoke about in all stars five how  the rose petal moment kind of affected  her  everywhere she went anything she did she  was very affected by that  um tell me as a friend shea is in  nightgowns forever  how did it feel to see her finally get  her crown  you know this is part of my my  like anti-capitalist drag i feel  is a resistance against like the idea of  one person winning a competition there's  really no place for that  like in in my vision of drag i've always  in my gowns i spoke to speak about like  i don't believe in the idea of a  reigning plane there should be a royal  court  and i think it is my greatest pleasure  to see  the top four of my season one by one  each get  the crowns that we have all deserved  from the beginning peppermint is a  hunter  next i mean i expect her to just go  ahead and win an emmy or tony instead  but the drag race crown is definitely  hers as well  the world feels better now that jay  coulee has a drag race crown  oh hey there if you want more lgbtq news  and exclusive interviews click  subscribe or watch these videos
 

